# ============================================================================
#  reference/ IS DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED. DO NOT "CLEAN THIS UP".
# ============================================================================
#  Everything under reference/ originates from third parties and MUST NOT
#  enter this repository's history:
#
#    reference/apk/        the original Magic Portals APK (Asantee Games)
#    reference/extracted/  unpacked APK contents — art, audio, scene/entity
#                          data. We have written permission to REBUILD the
#                          game and REUSE assets; we do NOT have permission
#                          to REDISTRIBUTE them, and a public git repo is
#                          redistribution.
#    reference/ethanon/    Ethanon Engine source (MIT). Vendoring it would be
#                          legal, but it is read-only decoding reference with
#                          its own upstream — it is cloned, not committed.
#                          (It also carries its own nested .git/.)
#
#  Git history is effectively permanent: a commit that lands here is a
#  licensing problem that a later `git rm` does not undo. Whoever is reading
#  this and considering an exception — don't. Put the file somewhere else.
#
#  Consequence, by design: a fresh clone has NO reference/ directory. See
#  README.md for how to recreate it locally.
#
#  DELIBERATELY UNANCHORED (no leading slash): this matches reference/ at ANY
#  depth, not just the repo root. The converter's default input path is
#  cwd-relative, so running it from tools/converter/ would create
#  tools/converter/reference/extracted/ — which a root-anchored "/reference/"
#  would NOT ignore. Do not "tidy" this by adding the slash back.
# ============================================================================
reference/


# --- Godot ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Import cache & editor-generated data. The Godot project root is game/, so in
# practice this is game/.godot/ — left unanchored anyway, for the same reason as
# reference/ above: a second Godot project anywhere in the tree should also be
# covered, and .godot/ is never something worth committing.
.godot/
# Exported builds (APK output — large, reproducible)
build/
/game/android/build/
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore
*.jks

# --- Python converter ----------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/

# --- Converter output staging --------------------------------------------
# The converter reads reference/extracted/ and writes .tscn/assets. Anything
# it emits that still carries Asantee-origin content (textures, audio, level
# data) is subject to the same rule as reference/ above. Keep generated
# output here and it stays out of history until it has been reviewed.
# Unanchored for the same reason as reference/ — the converter's default output
# path is cwd-relative, so out/ can appear below tools/converter/ too.
out/

# --- OS / editor cruft ---------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
